From c00dff8f76eebc4e502bfd83d6b47b5172d952c7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 21:07:54 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] Input: pm8xxx-vibrator - extract the upper drive byte
 with a right shift

PMI632-compatible hardware splits the millivolt drive value across an
eight-bit lower register and a four-bit upper field. Left-shifting the
value by drv2_shift before masking that field always writes zero.
For example, 2400 mV needs an upper field of 0x9, not zero.

Right-shift to extract the upper bits, preserving the existing lower
field and masked-write behavior. Legacy one-register variants do not
enter this path.

Codex (GPT-6) found and prepared this fix while extending the earlier
vibrator tests, which explicitly excluded upper-byte encoding. The
three existing fixes still fail 8160 expanded checks without this
change. The complete series passes 86077 checks over 12303 cases under
address, undefined-behavior and leak sanitizers; the upper-left control
reproduces those 8160 failures. ARM/ARM64 driver and FF-helper objects
compile with W=1 without diagnostics. The regmap/work services are
modeled; PMI632 hardware and full FF IOCTL behavior are not tested.

Fixes: 9e0631695eac ("input: pm8xxx-vibrator: add new SPMI vibrator support")

diff --git a/drivers/input/misc/pm8xxx-vibrator.c b/drivers/input/misc/pm8xxx-vibrator.c
index d4fdb5652584..661224de4ab2 100644
--- a/drivers/input/misc/pm8xxx-vibrator.c
+++ b/drivers/input/misc/pm8xxx-vibrator.c
@@ -119,7 +119,7 @@ static int pm8xxx_vib_set(struct pm8xxx_vib *vib, bool on)
 	vib->reg_vib_drv = val;
 
 	if (regs->drv2_mask) {
-		val = vib->level << regs->drv2_shift;
+		val = vib->level >> regs->drv2_shift;
 		rc = regmap_write_bits(vib->regmap, vib->drv2_addr,
 				regs->drv2_mask, on ? val : 0);
 		if (rc < 0)
